Error [jet.ComptimeConstructNotSupported]: `parsed` holds a compiler value (`CompilerSyntaxTree`), which exists only while compiling
  --> tests/ui/compiler_api/compiler_value_read_at_runtime_is_rejected.jet:7:11
    |
  7 |     print(parsed.items.len())
    |           ^^^^^^
 Why: Comptime code and `build: fn` read compiler values; the running program has no compiler to answer them
 Fix: Compute the plain value you need (a Bool, number or String) inside a `comptime` block and read that at runtime
More: jet-lang.dev/e/E0956
